WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:03.446
This briefing comes from
Access and Privilege,

3
00:00:03.446 --> 00:00:06.612
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:06.612 --> 00:00:09.774
Identity and Directory moved the identity,

5
00:00:09.774 --> 00:00:13.462
and HR-Driven Identity made
its facts trustworthy.

6
00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:17.387
This book is about what happens
with those facts on every sign-in:

7
00:00:17.387 --> 00:00:20.275
who gets access to what,
under which conditions,

8
00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:24.125
and how administrator power is
kept from becoming an open door.

9
00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:26.663
We'll take it through
why, what, who and how.

10
00:00:26.663 --> 00:00:32.075
And the short version is this: in Zero
Trust, every access decision is a policy

11
00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:37.401
decision, and the policy library is, in
practice, the agency's access control.

12
00:00:37.401 --> 00:00:38.710
Let's start with why.
